  "title": "Which contact laws see how rings continue",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "For rule-60 rings joined by contacts with self-blind laws c <- u(l_a, r_a) + v(l_b, r_b) (u, v any two-input tables, 256 laws): (1) re-routing at a contact changes the automaton exactly unless u and v are affine with equal coefficients of the arriving cell (32 blind laws, among them law (12,12)); (2) an affine law that sees the routing reads only one of the contact's arriving cells, so the other ring does not pass the contact; a law that sees the routing with both rings passing is nonlinear (128 laws); (3) under affine laws binding (A32) is needing both rings, under nonlinear laws it is stronger.",
